text.section:
Whenever a domestic business trust has adopted and approved, in the manner required by this article, a plan of domestication providing for the business trust to be domesticated under the laws of another jurisdiction, the business trust shall file with the Commission articles of trust surrender setting forth:

The name of the business trust;


The business trust's new jurisdiction of formation;


The business trust's new entity type, if any;


The plan of domestication;


A statement that the articles of trust surrender are being filed in connection with the domestication of the business trust as a foreign entity to be formed under the laws of another jurisdiction and that the business trust is surrendering its charter under the laws of this Commonwealth;


A statement that the plan was adopted by the business trust in accordance with § 13.1-1267;


A statement that the domestic business trust revokes the authority of its registered agent to accept service on its behalf and appoints the clerk of the Commission as its agent for service of process in any proceeding based on a cause of action arising during the time it was formed in this Commonwealth;


A mailing address to which the clerk may mail a copy of any process served on him under subdivision 7; and


A commitment to notify the clerk of the Commission in the future of any change in the mailing address of the business trust.
